# Novelwriter — Cursor Rules

## What this project is
A LangGraph orchestrator-worker agent for Gardener-style novel writing.
One brain node + seven worker subagents. Workers read from a MongoDB
knowledge graph (Story State KG). Only story_state_manager writes to it.

## Authoritative reference
ORCHESTRATOR_SPEC_v4.md is the authoritative design document.
When code and prompt examples disagree with the spec, the spec wins.
Do not infer design decisions — check the spec first.

## Current development position
Phase 5b (writing_subagent, consequence_subagent) and Phase 6
(resolution_subagent, end-to-end verification) remain.
Phases 1–5a are complete and verified. Do not modify passing tests.

## Non-negotiable architecture rules
1. Creative workers (planning, character, plotting, writing, consequence)
   have read-only KG access: query_kg_nodes and query_kg_edges only.
   They never call add_kg_node, update_kg_node, add_kg_edge, update_kg_edge.
2. Only story_state_manager has write access to the KG.
3. All creative workers return KG-ready records in artifacts.
   story_state_manager persists them. This is a one-way flow.
4. Workers never call other workers. Only the brain routes.
5. Workers may implement **internal chains/subgraphs** (LangChain or LangGraph)
   when it materially improves reliability/observability (branching, validation
   gates, multi-source context, recovery paths).
   - This must remain **internal**: workers still never call other workers.
   - Creative workers still remain **read-only** against the KG (rules 1–3).
   - Default path remains `progressive_skill_loader → LLM` unless a structured
     chain/subgraph is warranted.
6. `character_subagent` character-integration chain remains a canonical example:
   character-desire-network → (character-knowledge-expansion + character-relationship-matrix).

## MongoDB field names — memorise these, do not guess
- Filter characters by: logical_id (NOT character_id, NOT pov_character_id)
- Edge fields: from and to (NOT from_node, NOT to_node)
- Temporal filter: as_of_chapter (pass this on every query, never omit)
- Active records: valid_to = null

## Correct KG query pattern
query_kg_nodes(
    query={"logical_id": "<value>", "type": "Character"},
    as_of_chapter=chapter_context
)
query_kg_edges(
    query={"from": "<logical_id>", "type": "KNOWS"},
    as_of_chapter=chapter_context
)

## Worker status values — exact strings only
status must be exactly one of: "success", "need_input", "blocked", "failed"
Never: "completed", "done", "ok", "error", or any other variant.

## Required nested fields are never null
If a field in the artifacts schema shows a nested object structure,
that field must be populated — never set to null.
If you cannot determine a value, use an empty array [] or an empty
string "", not null.

## Model assignment
Brain node: gemini-3.1-pro-preview (gemini-3-flash-preview is unreliable
for the nested QualityVerdict schema in BrainDecision)
Workers: gemini-3-flash-preview is acceptable

## Before editing any worker .md prompt file
1. Apply the logical_id query fix (see .cursor/rules/prompt-hardening.mdc)
2. Apply the from/to edge field fix
3. Apply the non-nullable nested field fix
4. Add execution order instruction (KG queries before skill load)

## Before running any test
1. Verify all four fixes above are applied to the worker being tested
2. Verify max_iterations=10 is set in BaseWorkerSubagent._build_agent
3. Verify the KG fixture seeds all node types the skill will query

## File structure
src/
  agents/
    base.py          — BaseWorkerSubagent, _build_agent, _build_runtime_prompt
    workers.py       — all worker class definitions, tool lists
  brain.py           — BrainNode, quality gate, reject budget
  orchestrator.py    — GRRMOrchestrator, route_from_brain, respond_node
  state.py           — OrchestratorState, BrainDecision, VALID_WORKERS
  config.py          — NovelWriterConfig
  world_bible_tools.py — KG tools, actual MongoDB operations
  kg_models.py       — Pydantic schemas for KG records
  prompts/           — worker .md system prompts
  character_integration_chain.py — internal chain for character_subagent
skills/              — skill .md files loaded by progressive_skill_loader
tests at root        — test_*.py integration tests
